Repair only the supplied scientific or grammatical issues. Return {sections:[{id:number,patches:[{before:string,after:string,issueIndex:number}],reason:string}]}. Include each supplied section exactly once. Use exact unique substrings in its candidate. At most 3 non-overlapping patches per section; their combined BEFORE text must cover at most 35% of that section. issueIndex refers to that section's issues. Keep wording elsewhere unchanged. Restore the original meaning, uncertainty and proposal status. No extra style pass. If bounded repairs cannot solve the issues, return patches:[] and explain.
INPUT DATA:
{"sections": [{"id": 4, "heading": "Planned Evaluation", "original": "The evaluation will report boundary disagreement on observable terrain and the fraction of pixels left unresolved. Abstentions will be reported separately from correct classifications, so the system cannot appear accurate simply by declining most cases. We will also inspect examples in which a cloud edge resembles an ice boundary. These are planned comparisons, and no field measurements are yet available.", "candidate": "The evaluation will report boundary disagreement on observable terrain and the fraction of pixels left unresolved. Abstentions will be reported separately from correct classifications to ensure the system's accuracy is not inflated by avoiding difficult cases. We will also examine examples where a cloud edge closely resembles an ice boundary. These comparisons are planned, and no field measurements are currently available.", "issues": [{"originalQuote": "so the system cannot appear accurate simply by declining most cases", "revisedQuote": "to ensure the system's accuracy is not inflated by avoiding difficult cases", "problem": "Replaces the explicit safeguard against declining most cases with a claim about avoiding difficult cases. Difficulty is not the abstention criterion, and separate reporting does not ensure that selective avoidance cannot inflate accuracy."}]}, {"id": 5, "heading": "Limitations and Conclusion", "original": "An abstention rule may make the limits of the evidence clearer while leaving a less complete map. A local inventory may also contain outdated boundaries. The proposed experiment will therefore not estimate annual retreat rates or establish that any particular glacier is shrinking [S2]. Its contribution would be a more explicit account of what the available images can support.", "candidate": "An abstention rule may make the limits of the evidence clearer, albeit at the cost of a less complete map. A local inventory, however, may contain outdated boundaries. Consequently, the proposed experiment will not estimate annual retreat rates or definitively establish that any particular glacier is shrinking [S2]. Instead, its contribution lies in providing a more explicit account of what the available images can support.", "issues": [{"originalQuote": "or establish that any particular glacier is shrinking", "revisedQuote": "or definitively establish that any particular glacier is shrinking", "problem": "Adding 'definitively' weakens the stated limitation by leaving open that the experiment could establish glacier shrinkage less definitively."}, {"originalQuote": "Its contribution would be a more explicit account", "revisedQuote": "its contribution lies in providing a more explicit account", "problem": "Recasts a conditional, prospective contribution as an existing contribution, weakening the distinction between proposed and completed work."}, {"originalQuote": "A local inventory may also contain outdated boundaries.", "revisedQuote": "A local inventory, however, may contain outdated boundaries.", "problem": "'However' introduces an unsupported contrast with the preceding abstention tradeoff; this is an additional limitation."}]}], "sources": [{"id": "S1", "title": "Controlled source packet: domain and evidence brief", "excerpt": "The proposed glacier study uses optical imagery from two summer visits. Cloud-covered pixels are unavailable observations, not ice-free terrain. A local inventory supplies glacier outlines but does not establish recent retreat. No field measurements have been collected for this proposal.", "content_kind": "author_constructed_evaluation_fixture"}, {"id": "S2", "title": "Controlled source packet: experimental design brief", "excerpt": "A boundary model will receive the same image pairs in both conditions. The comparison is between mandatory classification and an abstention rule for cloud-covered pixels. The evaluation set will contain 24 image pairs. The study will not estimate annual retreat rates.", "content_kind": "author_constructed_evaluation_fixture"}]}
